g his big brother from this  truth  with those facts out in the open dom is  more open to reconciling with jacob  which is very convenient for when otto  betrays the younger toretto  siding with cypher and attempting to  take jacob off the board  in the heat of the film's elaborate  climax jacob whose sister mia has helped  him escape  returns to the fray to help his  brother's new family foiled the  world-shattering caper he himself  initially conceived  stopping otto's implementation of aries  on the ground with the toretto family  fully reunited is just one half of the  strategy while dom jacob mia and the  others try to bring down the armored  truck housing aries and stop it from  uploading its code to a satellite in  orbit  tej and roman have to thwart things on  the other side of the transfer in outer  orbit  space the final frontier  the idea that the gang would end up  traveling in space gets seeded early in  two key ways  firstly roman's arc throughout f9 is  vaguely meta-textual  as he becomes obsessed with how many  harrowing experiences a cast  collectively survives and how rarely  they wind up even lightly scarred  he begins to believe that maybe just  maybe they all might be in some way  invincible  at the same time tej and roman are sent  to germany to acquire wheels and gear  for the mission  and there they cross paths with a trio  of tokyo drift stars  sean twinkie and earl the trio now  developed cars that are  wouldn't you guess strapped with massive  rockets so when it comes time to try to  disable a satellite that ramsay can't  hack from the ground  roman and tedge have to suit up in  diving gear and duct tape and  subsequently blast off into space  but their original plan of frying the  satellite with an emp fails their only  remaining option is to destroy the  satellite with brute force  which would require them to use the last  of their rocket fuel to propel their  modded car ship through the craft  which would also strand them in space  with no way home this is where roman's  invincibility obsession comes into play  as he makes his peace with the idea that  either they will somehow miraculously  survive this ridiculous situation or  this will be their last stand  what better way to go out he posits than  to die in space  roman's thesis is essentially proven  correct when their hail mary play saves  the day and a foreign space crew finds  them and helps them back to earth  with the bad guys beaten and the toretto  family wounds beginning to heal things  can return to normal  or as normal as dom's gang can ever  truly have  throughout f9 mia and letty both  struggle with accepting time away from  the fast-paced lifestyle of their  previous movies  they're both mothers now two women who  have otherwise never had solo dialogue  together on all these films get time to  bond on screen in f9 and both find that  it's okay to no longer throw themselves  into the fray but agree that they can't  hide away from adventure when it comes  to their doorstep  when the whole gang gets together for  the obligatory corona sponsored cookout  at the old toretto home now being  rebuilt after the last film's  destruction the crew is back home in la  and no longer hiding abroad  they even leave a seat at the table for  brian o'connor whose car speeds up the  driveway just as the credits roll  after this there will be a fast ten two  parts of it in fact as deadline reports  as eventful as f9 is the film's  conclusion leaves a few tasty open  threads to be untangled in that  double-fisted finale  fast and furious this isn't a movie it's  tradition for the second film in a row  cypher gets away scot-free  while plenty of other antagonists in the  fast franchise have received redemption  arcs and second chances it's unlikely  that the woman who killed the mother of  dom's child is going to get off so  easily  as for han he is alive and back in the  fold but as a mid-credits teaser reminds  us he still has unfinished business with 